title CAUM5 — the carry meets: a committed device run lands in the desk inbox
prompt recur the 1024-round itinerary Lindy-first crux-first; take the next agent-doable lap on the road past BUHR, self-approve design rounds, send each finished increment as its own signed round, stop at custody gates
think CAUM3 proved the sending hand (record → commit → wire frame) and CAUM4 proved the receiving hand (deframe verify-before-trust → keep only what is proven whole). Each hand was witnessed alone; the two had never been shown meeting. Lindy-first crux-first, the most durable next move is not a sixth new surface but the join of the two proven ones — the SETU Glass↔Desk carry names exactly this shape.
think The crux is the composition held to the forgetting promise across the seam: a recorded, committed run lands byte-for-byte, and ONLY such a run does. Every refusal is inherited, not re-implemented — NothingToCarry from the sending hand, the six deframe errors from the receiving hand. The join adds one invariant of its own: a clean carry leaves the desk holding the device's committed bytes and nothing else.
think mikrophone/carry.rye composes firmware.carry_frame and inbox.accept over their public APIs, inventing no transport, no buffer, no new error. carry_to_inbox frames the recorder's committed carry then accepts it verify-before-trust; a forgotten run refuses NothingToCarry at the frame step so the inbox is never touched.
obs The sharp end-to-end invariants: an uncommitted tail (commit keep, feed X, stop) carries exactly keep; a forgotten run refuses NothingToCarry and a prior keep in the inbox is left untouched (neither lands nor erases); a payload byte flipped in transit refuses DigestMismatch and the desk keeps nothing while a prior good keep still stands; and both hands forget whole — device working buffer zero after power_down, desk inbox zero after clear (buffer checked byte-for-byte).
obs Custody untouched — the single wire is still a byte slice handed function to function; the Sha256 stays an integrity check the receiver recomputes, not a signature. Real hardware, a real cable, a real desk stay custody gate #2; no custody gate reached this round.
